On Nov 12, 6:45 am, alan <almkg...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Right now I think I need BoH and ring of FA.

Neither is necessary for ascension, and =FA is particularly optional
(it is only important if someone throws a !paralysis at you on Astral;
it's very nice then, but that's not a really common occurrence and
isn't necessarily lethal without FA if you're well prepared).  But BoH
is such a convenience that I find it worth expending some effort/
resources to get.

>  However since I'm
> atheist (and hence no risk of getting an artifact from my god) I'm
> wondering if I should get yet another artifact before I complete my
> quest.  My options are either the Orb of Detection or the Magic Mirror
> of Merlin.  I think Orb of Detection is better.

Jumping boots would be higher on my list than either of those, also
markers and switching to leather gloves (or dex if you find them, but
that's not a big deal).  You've got ESP and MR already.

Really at this point I'd be going for as many markers as possible.
Get the AC down, and keep a lot of outs and conveniences available.

> 1.  You have to keep track of resistances, really.  I tended to lose

/enlightenment helps here.

> track of them, because somewhere along the way I would pray so much
> that I'd be crowned, which gives all the important resistances.  For
> example, I thought I could still bop Medusa even though she had a wand
> of lightning - but I forgot that I didn't have shock resistance.

You have reflection now, so really only fire resistance (for gehennom)
and sleep/poison are mandatory though the others are nice vs. vortices
and such.

> 2.  You really, really have to avoid bad situations.  I thought I was
> able to do that, but it turns out I'm a little too reliant on my god's
> get-out-of-bad-situation-free card.  Going atheist forced me to stand
> behind my pet, even at early stages, so that he would be powerful
> enough to have a go at the Minetown watchmen and I could pick through
> their armor.

Elbereth.  Keep /fire in main inventory (for E), with /teleport and /
digging as backups.  You shouldn't really be relying on prayer past
the very early game in a regular game, and even then only when
spamming E fails.

> 3.  Priest's HP growth sucks, so standing behind pets is really a good
> idea regardless of theism or lack thereof.

Pets are good, just don't be too reliant on them to the point where
having them get levelported/trap doored/polymorphed/etc is a massive
problem.  Having several helps mitigate those risks.



